    "Solutions Use Case NAS Storage Solutions Gaming Storage RAID Storage Solutions Video Surveillance Storage Backup & Recovery Solutions Enterprise & Data Center Storage Content Creation & Media Storage Compare & Learn HDD vs. SSD AI Storage Infrastructure Data Security & Encryption Compare Hard Drives Thunderbolt vs. USB-C Industries Healthcare Education Hybrid Cloud Explore how our storage solutions support real-world use cases—from personal backups to enterprise infrastructure. View All Solutions & Use Cases",
    "Support Help Topics Support Home Software Downloads Product Registration Warranty Services Data Recovery Services Order Status Order Status Returns & Replacements Product Security FAQs Contact Support Chat With Us Call Us Email Us Need help from an expert? Chat with our support team for help with orders, warranty questions, troubleshooting, or to connect with a representative. Live Chat with Support SanDisk Professional hard drives are now G-DRIVE. Support and Product Information are still available, just under a new name.",
    "Company About Us Overview Innovation Our Locations Careers Investors Capital Corporate Responsibility Overview Sustainability People Supply Chain Ethics Philanthropy Data Privacy News & Events Newsroom Press Releases Events Blog Posts Shopping for business? Join our business program today to get tiered pricing, rewards for your purchases, and more exclusive benefits. See All Benefits Sign Up Now Tiered Pricing for Business Members Get special rates on select products. New products added monthly. p.nav-promo-tiered-pricing { background-image: url(\"https://www.westerndigital.com/content/dam/store/en-us/assets/business/icons/icon-tiered-pricing-53.png\"); background-repeat: no-repeat; padding-left: 67px; padding-top: 5px; min-height: 60px; } See All Products with Tiered Pricing",
    "Can’t find your product? Choose by category.",
    "Western Digital has separated into two independent companies and the support process for your Western Digital and Sandisk brand HDD and flash products may have changed. Need help with flash products, SSDs and memory cards, go to Sandisk Support.",
    "Software Downloads",
    "Returns & Replacements",
    "Warranty Services",
    "Product Registration",
    "Order Status",
    "FAQs",
    "Western Digital Support How-To Videos",
    "Visit Us on Our Channel",
    "You can go to our Software Download page and look for the software or firmware there.",
    "Product Coverage Western Digital Support handles Hard Disk Drives (Desktop, Portable & Internal) and Platform products (Data Center & Servers). SanDisk Support covers flash-based products like Solid-State Drives (SSDs) and flash memory.",
    "Accessing SanDisk Support If you registered a flash product before September 25, 2024, a SanDisk Support account was created using your Western Digital Support email. The same password applies but can be reset anytime. If you registered a product but did not complete the setup of your account, click ‘Forgot Password’ on the Support sign in screen, and enter the email address associated with your registered product.",
    "Account Linking Accounts are separate and tied to different companies. Changes to one account (profile info, updates) will not sync with the other.",
    "Account Information Western Digital Support shows your HDD and platform product registrations and support cases. SanDisk Support shows your flash product registrations and support cases.",
    "All warranty claims must be submitted through your Western Digital Support account. Please have your product’s serial number ready.",
    "If you have a support account, log into your Support Account. If your product is already registered, click Warranty Replacement> Get Started and then select the product. If your product is not registered, click Warranty Replacement > Get Started, then choose Register a New Product before proceeding.",
    "If your product is already registered, click Warranty Replacement> Get Started and then select the product.",
    "If your product is not registered, click Warranty Replacement > Get Started, then choose Register a New Product before proceeding.",
    "If you don’t have a support account, create a support account here.",
    "You will need to log in to your support account and have your warranty replacement number ready. Option 1",
    "On WesternDigital.com, click Support > Warranty Service > Warranty Replacement Status > Enter your warranty replacement number to view the status.",
    "Alternatively, from the Support Home Page, scroll down to the “Warranty Service” tile and follow the same steps.",
    "Option 2",
    "On product support account overview page, click “warranty replacement” from the side panel, then select “Check Status”.",
    "It is not required to have an account or log in to check your warranty status.",
    "On westerndigital.com, click “Support” > “Warranty Services” > “Warranty Status”.",
    "Alternatively, from the Support Home Page, scroll down to the “Warranty Service” tile and follow the same steps.",
    "If you’re unsure where to find the Serial Number, refer to the label on the product or check your device settings, depending on the product type.",
    "Find solutions for your external drive detection issues: Windows: https://support-en.wd.com/app/answers/detailweb/a_id/52804 Mac: https://support-en.wd.com/app/answers/detailweb/a_id/52805",
    "If you're a new customer (no support account yet)",
    "Use the registration link in your shipping confirmation email or order details page. After registering, you’ll receive an email to set up your support account.",
    "Alternatively, visit our Support Website and select “Product Registration”.",
    "You can also use our Chatbot on the website for step-by-step guidance.",
    "If you already have a support account",
    "Log in to your account.",
    "Go to “Registered Products” > “Register a New Product” or scroll down and click “Register a New Product” from the relevant section.",
    "If you have a backup from the data, reformat the drive and restore data from the back up.",
    "If you don’t have a backup from the data, please do the data recovery, check this article for the details. https://support-en.wd.com/app/answers/detailweb/a_id/18754",
    "Mac users can use FirstAid (build-in) app to try to recover it but if that doesn’t work, please send the drive to Data Recovery. Please check this article for more details. https://support-en.wd.com/app/answers/detailweb/a_id/50200",
    "Reach out to Support for more assistance.",
